# to [[crack]], to [[break]] (of the voice)
# {{lb|ru|colloquial}} to [[pose]], to [[mince]], to [[pretend]]
#: {{syn|ru|выла́мываться|кривля́ться}}
#: {{pf|ru|полома́ться|q1=only}}
# {{lb|ru|colloquial}} to [[be]] [[obstinate]], to cause difficulties, to [[refuse]] to agree
#: {{syn|ru|выла́мываться|отне́киваться}}
#: {{ux|ru|[[он|Он]] [[до́лго]] '''лома́лся''', [[но]] [[пото́м]] [[мы]] [[он|его́]] [[уговорить|уговори́ли]] [[пойти́]] [[с]] [[вы|на́ми]].|He was pigheaded for a long time but then we convinced him to come with us.}}
#: {{pf|ru|полома́ться|q1=only}}
# {{infl of|ru|лома́ть||pass}}

====Usage notes====
The perfective {{m|ru|слома́ться}} refers to one single complete act, while [[abstract verb|abstract]] {{m|ru|полома́ться}} refers to a complete stretch of either multiple acts or a continuous act.

